# Shared UI & shell

## App modes (`App.jsx`)

- `sessionStorage` key `scanlogic_app_mode`: `suite` | `scanvault`.
- Share links force ScanVault mode.

## Suite shell

- `Dashboard.jsx` — tab state: `docs`, `tax`, `docdraft`, `contracts`, `lawyer`, `settings`.
- `AppShell.jsx` variants: `suite` vs ScanVault.
- `TabBar.jsx` / `ResponsiveNav.jsx` — bottom/side nav; `layoutId="suite-tab"` for animations.
- `PremiumModal.jsx` + `PremiumContext.jsx` — `localStorage` premium flag.

## Contexts

| Context | File | Purpose |
|---------|------|---------|
| Auth | `AuthContext.jsx` | Suite user stub from appApi.auth |
| Premium | `PremiumContext.jsx` | Trial/premium modal |
| Guide | `GuideContext.jsx` | App guide drawer open/focus |
| AI language | `AiLanguageContext.jsx` | Global DE/EN for all LLM surfaces (`useAiLanguage`) |

## In-app guide

- Content: `lib/guide/appModules.js` — **source of truth** for module descriptions.
- UI: `GuideFab`, `AppGuideDrawer`, `ModuleGuideBanner`, `invokeAppGuide.js`.
- When changing a module’s user-facing purpose, update `APP_GUIDE_MODULES` entries.

## Settings (`SettingsPage.jsx`)

- User-facing: AI language, app guide, PWA install, optional cloud sign-in, ScanVault link, Tax Vault settings, Premium.
- Server config (Anthropic, DATABASE_URL, LAN secret) lives in `.env` only — not exposed in Settings UI.
- One-time local→Supabase migration: use `pushAllLocalDataToSupabase` from dev console or a script if needed.

## PWA

- `lib/pwa/register.js`, `InstallPwaButton.jsx`, `usePwaInstall.js`.
- Config in `vite.config.js` `VitePWA` — do not enable dev SW (`devOptions.enabled: false`).

## Styling

- Tailwind 4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`; global `index.css`.
- Mobile: `safe-top`, `min-h-[48px]` touch targets, `rounded-2xl` cards.
- Framer Motion for tab transitions in Dashboard.

## Patterns

```jsx
// ✅ Optional guide hook in nav
const guide = useGuideOptional()

// ✅ Toast feedback
import { toast } from 'sonner'
```

## Do not

- Break `GuideProvider` wrapping when adding new suite tabs — pass `activeModule` id matching `appModules.js`.
- Store premium or API secrets in `VITE_*` env vars.
